{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1220291-potential-gifts-for-the-anurana","id":1220291,"title":"Potential Gifts for the Anurana","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-05-19T11:43:15-07:00","id":1220291,"title":"Potential Gifts for the Anurana","content":"Assuming that the Anurana acquire the patronage of spirits, what sort of themes should their Gift list cover, outside of physically froggy things like jumping, croaking, poisons, etc.?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-19T14:42:42-07:00","id":1220338,"title":"","content":"Well, water-related activities, like holding one's breath or breathing underwater, for one. Also remember there are also tree frogs, so properly re-skinned versions of gifts like City Running would be appropriate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;At the risk of sounding like a murder hobo&quot;<br /> <br /> Attributed to Nyrufa.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24134-inertial-frame","name":"Inertial Frame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-19T17:53:04-07:00","id":1220374,"title":"","content":"I'd go also with a gift similar to Venom Blood, but also applies only to bite attacks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-19T18:42:52-07:00","id":1220390,"title":"","content":"Depends on who their patron is to be honest. I would include summing corrupted water spirits, controlling the water around them, bringing down the rain. I would give them a gift like the Gnawer Rank 4 gift, Infest, but I would call it Plague of Frogs. Frogs are also known in mythology to be a symbol of fertility, I might give them one of the Apis gifts that help them to increase the probability that they breed true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-19T20:16:32-07:00","id":1220409,"title":"","content":"Could also jump into amphibians in general, gifts like Grandmother's Touch and Combat healing as a pull from creatures like axolotl","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T15:51:17-07:00","id":1220640,"title":"","content":"They also have 4 fomori-like powers in Dagon, so gifts that allow them to us those powers in other forms. Could also have gifts that make those abilities stronger.<br /> <br /> A good example would be something like Prehensile Tongue which would function like Monkey Tail (Lupus, Rank 3) which grants Frog Tongue more usability. With a partial transformation, they could use their tongue and the gift in other forms as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T15:56:03-07:00","id":1220641,"title":"","content":"What about different gifts that let them do things with skin secretions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T16:35:16-07:00","id":1220650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1220291-potential-gifts-for-the-anurana?p=1220641#post1220641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about different gifts that let them do things with skin secretions?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this falls under &quot;physically froggy&quot; gifts. I was thinking of Croaking gifts myself lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T17:06:06-07:00","id":1220660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1220291-potential-gifts-for-the-anurana?p=1220650#post1220650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think this falls under &quot;physically froggy&quot; gifts. I was thinking of Croaking gifts myself lol.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Fair, I was trying to think more specific that's all...could also expand it to amphibians in general. Get some extreme axlotl inspired regeneration. Do fun things like rage heal easier, or get to rip your tongue off after tying someone up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-06T09:49:09-07:00","id":1225325,"title":"","content":"I dunno about tongue-ripping; seems a bit too Wyrmish, body-horror-y to me. But then, there's a real-world frog that breaks the bones in its front legs so the shattered ends break out of its skin so as to use them as claws, so I suppose it's all relative...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-06T13:50:25-07:00","id":1225442,"title":"","content":"Well....the Anurana are are of the wyrm","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-09T18:45:12-07:00","id":1226156,"title":"","content":"I disagree. Created by the Wyrm's minions, yes, but not of it any more than a BSD before they go through the spiral.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-09T19:49:38-07:00","id":1226164,"title":"","content":"The book talks about how they need polluted water to pass the gauntlet and how the details of their reproduction stop them from staying away from polluted water....not exactly pre-spiral dance cub condition. They even attack people who try to cleanse their waters. You could run an arc where they get cleansed sure...but the cannon is running on the idea that at their core the Mockery Breeds are of the Wyrm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-10T04:24:32-07:00","id":1226222,"title":"","content":"Thing is they are not a result of a Godly Miracle from Celestines, they are manmade abominations that are slightly less abominable then other creations. If they manage to uplift themselves, I would still have taint as a big part of their character, as well as being less potent then Natural Fera. Think about it, if Archmages usually can't create a viable shapeshifter from scratch I am not expecting Pentext to outdo them.<br /> <br /> A good reference would be I Hate All Life's Debased homebrew, the Dog Shifters. Basically they are a universally metis breed of Dog Shifters, with stunted spirits. This would be the most ideal situation these froggies can hope for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-10T07:07:44-07:00","id":1226238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1220291-potential-gifts-for-the-anurana?p=1226222#post1226222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A good reference would be I Hate All Life's Debased homebrew, the Dog Shifters.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't happen to still has access to that homebrew writeup do you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-10T09:24:32-07:00","id":1226254,"title":"","content":"I was a fan of the Debased as well...kept kicking around using them in one of my games. I thought they'd be a fun curve ball for the players (esp since they aren't in any cannon books I'm the only one in my group to know about them...a surprise for once).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-14T19:15:52-07:00","id":1260606,"title":"","content":"I've done some thinking, and here are some ideas for Gifts:<br /> <br /> Frog-ness (swimming, jumping, metamorphosis): <b>(1)</b> Shed; Frog Hop [as Lupus Gift: Hare\u2019s Leap]; Summon Feast [as Bone Gnawer Gift: Scent of Sweet Honey]; The Innsmouth Look [as Homid Gift: Mark of the Wolf, reflects semi-illusory unpleasant appearance]; Sticky Tongue [as Silver Fang Gift: Falcon\u2019s Grasp, but only applies to use of the Frog Tongue power]; Cling [as Uktena Gift: Spirit of the Lizard]; Camouflage [as Wendigo Gift]; <b>(2)</b> Hop Frog [as Fianna Gift: Flame Dance]; Gender Shift [as Black Fury Gift: Man\u2019s Skin]; Gulp [as Rokea General Gift]; <b>(3)</b> Patagia [as Black Spiral Dancer Gift, taught by Flying Frog]; Great Leap [as Silent Strider Gift]; The Second Plague [as Camazotz Gift: Thousand Wing Form, except the Crawlerling-type body can swim and is made of frogs]; <b>(4)</b> Cocoon [as Homid Gift]; Doppelganger [as Glass Walker Gift]; <b>(5)</b> Protean Form [as Metis Gift];<br /> <br /> Sound (frog-calls): <b>(1)</b> Call of the Wyld; <b>(2)</b> Call of the Wyrm; Distractions; Ominous Croaking [as Galliard Gift: Howls in the Night]; <b>(3)</b> Song of the Siren; <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-14T19:26:32-07:00","id":1260611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1220291-potential-gifts-for-the-anurana?p=1260606#post1260606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've done some thinking, and here are some ideas for Gifts:<br /> <br /> Frog-ness (swimming, jumping, metamorphosis): <b>(1)</b> Shed; Frog Hop [as Lupus Gift: Hare\u2019s Leap]; Summon Feast [as Bone Gnawer Gift: Scent of Sweet Honey]; The Innsmouth Look [as Homid Gift: Mark of the Wolf, reflects semi-illusory unpleasant appearance]; Sticky Tongue [as Silver Fang Gift: Falcon\u2019s Grasp, but only applies to use of the Frog Tongue power]; Cling [as Uktena Gift: Spirit of the Lizard]; Camouflage [as Wendigo Gift]; <b>(2)</b> Hop Frog [as Fianna Gift: Flame Dance]; Gender Shift [as Black Fury Gift: Man\u2019s Skin]; Gulp [as Rokea General Gift]; <b>(3)</b> Patagia [as Black Spiral Dancer Gift, taught by Flying Frog]; Great Leap [as Silent Strider Gift]; The Second Plague [as Camazotz Gift: Thousand Wing Form, except the Crawlerling-type body can swim and is made of frogs]; <b>(4)</b> Cocoon [as Homid Gift]; Doppelganger [as Glass Walker Gift]; <b>(5)</b> Protean Form [as Metis Gift];<br /> <br /> Sound (frog-calls): <b>(1)</b> Call of the Wyld; <b>(2)</b> Call of the Wyrm; Distractions; Ominous Croaking [as Galliard Gift: Howls in the Night]; <b>(3)</b> Song of the Siren;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually, very happy with this list and will be co-opting it for my own games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-15T07:10:55-07:00","id":1260662,"title":"","content":"Glad you like it. I also have this:<br /> <br /> Poison: <b>(1)</b> Five Venoms Kin [as Ananasi Gift: Wyrmling Kinship]; Resist Toxin [as Bone Gnawer Gift]; <b>(2)</b> Poison Flesh [as Get of Fenris Gift: Venom Blood, save that it poisons anyone that bites the werefrog; <b>(3)</b> Dazzle [as Children of Gaia Gift, representing being high/intoxicated]; <b>(4)</b> Crawling Poison [as Black Spiral Dancer Gift]; Serenity [as Children of Gaia Gift, representing being stoned out of your gourd];<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-15T11:03:20-07:00","id":1260700,"title":"","content":"So what type of patron do you imagine uplifted them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-15T14:30:59-07:00","id":1260750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1220291-potential-gifts-for-the-anurana?p=1260700#post1260700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what type of patron do you imagine uplifted them?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Is it too cliche to just go with Frog? Could be the result of Garou assistance who feel cleansing these little C.H.U.D.s as a form of penance for the War of Rage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-15T16:44:27-07:00","id":1260771,"title":"","content":"I was partial to the idea of Haha no Fukami, the 'uncorrupted' Yama Queen who punishes crimes against/with flames and water. See <u>The 1000 Hells</u> for her full write-up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":665,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","user":"shkspr1048","date":". 10-15-2018, 07:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-15T16:57:12-07:00","id":1260774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1220291-potential-gifts-for-the-anurana?p=1260771#post1260771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was partial to the idea of Haha no Fukami, the 'uncorrupted' Yama Queen who punishes crimes against/with flames and water. See <u>The 1000 Hells</u> for her full write-up.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess that part maters more on where you want to center your game. A Yama Queen makes them specifically Eastern, while Frog could be anywhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","user":"CeltSPZ","date":". 10-15-2018, 08:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-15T17:20:08-07:00","id":1260781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1220291-potential-gifts-for-the-anurana?p=1260774#post1260774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I guess that part matters more on where you want to center your game.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. Another idea I had was the Anurana being backed by Cthulhu, because of the Lovecraft references in their write-up. Not the literal Great Old One, mind you, but a High Umbral spirit representative of the Mythos. Something just appeals to me about having a post-modern Totem for a post-modern Breed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-15T17:21:48-07:00","id":1260782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1220291-potential-gifts-for-the-anurana?p=1260781#post1260781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True. Another idea I had was the Anurana being backed by Cthulhu, because of the Lovecraft references in their write-up. Not the literal Great Old One, mind you, but a High Umbral spirit representative of the Mythos. Something just appeals to me about having a post-modern Totem for a post-modern Breed.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Don't think Cthulhu would be Wyrm?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-15T17:57:46-07:00","id":1260791,"title":"","content":"Three points:<br /> 1. I think he'd be too proud to submit to Wyrmish authority. He and the Anurana wouldn't be innocent, but rather...differently guilty.<br /> <br /> 2. Even if the Breed is collectively brought into the fold of spiritual recognition, they don't need to be all that observant. Call it the Esoteric Order of Dagon, Reformed.<br /> <br /> 3. It's a game where the protagonists are werewolves, and berserkers to boot. I say there's some wiggle room if it makes for a good game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-16T00:39:34-07:00","id":1260849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1220291-potential-gifts-for-the-anurana?p=1260774#post1260774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I guess that part maters more on where you want to center your game. A Yama Queen makes them specifically Eastern, while Frog could be anywhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well not necessarily... I mean you can have Uktena or Fenris and be a pack in Africa. A Yama Kong\u2019s main territory is in Asia, but it could spread out. It could also represent the Courts of the Emerald Mother could have been the ones to emancipate them.<br /> <br /> <br /> What about instead of Frog as singular you use the different aspects of Frog, or the Amphibian Kingdom, with a definite emphasis on the theme of Frogs association with Metamorphosis. So Tree Frog for Jungle totem, Cane Frog for ravager and herald of gluttony and extinction, Salamander for a fire and water mix, Arrow Frog for lethality. Like coyote has the faces of the Trickster, you could do a Parlament of Amphibians. As they channel Frog as a symbol of Change to essentially choose a destiny not limited as a bastard spawn of the Wyrm. So their Totem could be like their Auspice, they share a breed, like Corax sharing Breed gifts, and they haven\u2019t developed full on different tribes like Ajaba but develop individual brood cultures, with a Brood being composed of Anurana of different Totems, or Metamorph.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-16T03:39:20-07:00","id":1260878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1220291-potential-gifts-for-the-anurana?p=1260849#post1260849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well not necessarily... I mean you can have Uktena or Fenris and be a pack in Africa. A Yama Kong\u2019s main territory is in Asia, but it could spread out. It could also represent the Courts of the Emerald Mother could have been the ones to emancipate them.<br /> <br /> <br /> What about instead of Frog as singular you use the different aspects of Frog, or the Amphibian Kingdom, with a definite emphasis on the theme of Frogs association with Metamorphosis. So Tree Frog for Jungle totem, Cane Frog for ravager and herald of gluttony and extinction, Salamander for a fire and water mix, Arrow Frog for lethality. Like coyote has the faces of the Trickster, you could do a Parlament of Amphibians. As they channel Frog as a symbol of Change to essentially choose a destiny not limited as a bastard spawn of the Wyrm. So their Totem could be like their Auspice, they share a breed, like Corax sharing Breed gifts, and they haven\u2019t developed full on different tribes like Ajaba but develop individual brood cultures, with a Brood being composed of Anurana of different Totems, or Metamorph.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to disagree with the first half of the post. Sure you can have people migrate, but White Wolf put a lot of effort in &quot;othering&quot; Asia and Asian culture while putting Garou everywhere and making it possible for any tribe to pop up wherever you can find members of the Garou nation. This is something that always bothered me about WoD. It always read like West is West and East is East in an effort to make the East come off as mysterious, different and more of an Anime or Kung Fu film then a part of the same world that the Garou and Kindred run in. When it does talk about character using the Asian themed splats in the West it tends to mention places with stereotypical Asian populations to the American mind (LA, Hawaii, NYC). <br /> <br /> The second paragraph however I think has tons of room for fun. That would lead in time to a very fleshed out Frog culture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}